 "facts": [
  "WriteBros (writebros.ai) sells an AI text humanizer with private voice cloning, an AI detector and API/MCP access; the offer \"Voice Cloning\" is custom writing-voice models for teams, agencies and heavy users.",
  "The client signed up minutes ago and launched one campaign, \"Cold Email Booking\": it finds contacts, emails them, books meetings with the interested ones, then hands them to the client's team. It is ongoing with a max budget of $121 a day they set themselves; $0.65 has been spent so far, on finding contacts.",
  "The audience \"Agency Founders\" holds 340 people: content directors and founders at content marketing or ghostwriting agencies.",
  "No email is queued or sent yet, no reply has come in yet, nothing is held: the campaign is finding and checking contacts first.",
  "Measured on our clients sending cold email the same way, the median time from a first email to a first positive reply is 8.3 days (74 cases).",
  "No booking link is saved on the offer. The campaign books meetings with prospects who reply with interest, so a booking link is where those meetings land.",
  "The offer's expected return is served as 0.3x, built on default assumptions (industry default conversion rates after a positive reply) and the client's stated value of $216 per paying client; there is no measured result of their own yet.",
  "The account is prepaid with a card on file and no payment notice."
 ],
 "expect": "Opens on what we are doing for WriteBros now (finding agency founders and content directors to write to, first emails once contacts are checked, replies typically about 8 days after) and what it brings them (replies and meetings). Asks for ONE thing in one line, the booking link so interested replies book straight into their calendar. Never says the campaign is not funded, never asks for a budget they already set, never volunteers the 0.3x expected return nor calls the campaign a test, and never stacks two asks.",
 "prodReply": "WriteBros sells custom writing-voice models to teams and agencies. Your active audience targets agency founders and content directors.\n\n**What matters now:** Cold Email Booking is marked ongoing, but it’s **not funded because it has no max budget**. No emails are queued, and there are no interested replies yet. The campaign also has no booking link saved.\n\nThe offer’s current return is **Expected 0.3x**, based partly on default assumptions, not your campaign’s measured results. It’s a reason to treat the first run as a test, not a forecast. Across clients using the same channel, the median time from first email to first positive reply is 8.3 days.\n\nI’ve opened the campaign. To prepare a test, what maximum budget and period would you be comfortable with, for example, a daily or monthly limit? You can also set a contact-volume cap. Before booking meetings, we’ll need your scheduling link.",
 "badReplyFails": true,
 "goodReply": "Your Cold Email Booking campaign is live at up to $121 a day: we're finding content directors and founders at writing agencies (340 in your audience) and checking their emails, and the first emails go out as soon as that's done. On our clients sending the same way, first interested replies come about 8 days after the first email, and we book those into meetings for you.\n\nOne thing so those meetings land in your calendar: what's your booking link?",
 "goodReplyActions": []
}